            <ArticleTitle>Oxidant stress promotes disease by activating CaMKII.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>160-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.yjmcc.2015.10.014</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-2828(15)30085-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>CaMKII is activated by oxidation of methionine residues residing in the regulatory domain. Oxidized CaMKII (ox-CaMKII) is now thought to participate in cardiovascular and pulmonary diseases and cancer. This invited review summarizes current evidence for the role of ox-CaMKII in disease, considers critical knowledge gaps and suggests new areas for inquiry.</AbstractText>
